#{[17592186429952 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\text{ only}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186429952 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429952 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7f2e036f-6092-5f13-88cc-76a83386c5e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429955 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2k \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix},\\,k\\in R" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186429955 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429955 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e832ba8e-38d6-539c-9e5d-09409711b42c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186429955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f226cae3-dc9e-52a4-84a0-4560715ab839" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429959 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429959 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333779" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429959 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429959 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)-6y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives all equilibrium points of the system of linear differential equations above?" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186429959 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b59bb2fc-6ce1-5b76-9a55-8b95129f4121" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429959 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nThe equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-6y &=0 \\\\ x-2y &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNotice that the first equation is a multiple of the second one:\n\n$$\n3(x-2y)=3x-6y,\n$$\n\nso we can disregard the first equation.\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2y=0\\,⇒\\,x=2y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium points are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2k \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix},\\,k\\in R.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546274 #edb/ref 1080 "$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546274 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546274 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0cea3552-0e9d-56f2-9e24-8d9c17e4c552" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546277 #edb/ref 1080 "images/af/af8a897bcc199d1f07332d6d8dd26cd7d6173943378777d72246909e89d7837b.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546277 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546277 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e45555c-a01b-528d-b0e7-37a8317e6e4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546324 #edb/ref 1080 "images/af/af8a897bcc199d1f07332d6d8dd26cd7d6173943378777d72246909e89d7837b.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546324 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546324 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "21f20628-065b-591f-be75-7e55983b7906" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546332 #edb/ref 1080 "images/06/06b9fd74afcc99a3396aa280b248272904c495d6181e6a5c027c0cd6a30acbfb.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546332 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [